<article class="env-example" id="01KX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01KX">Example <span data-tag="01KX">26.21.17</span>.</a> Consider the nonaffine scheme $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k[x, y]) \setminus \{ (x, y)\} $ of Example <a href="/tag/01IL" data-tag="01IL">26.9.3</a>. On the other hand, consider the scheme </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathbf{GL}_{2, k} = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k[a, b, c, d, 1/ad - bc]).  \]
</div>
  <p> There is a morphism $\mathbf{GL}_{2, k} \to U$ corresponding to the ring map $x \mapsto a$, $y \mapsto b$. It is easy to see that this is a surjective morphism, and hence the image is not contained in any affine open of $U$. In fact, the affine scheme $\mathbf{GL}_{2, k}$ also surjects onto $\mathbf{P}^1_ k$, and $\mathbf{P}^1_ k$ does not even have an immersion into <em>any</em> affine scheme. </p>
</article>